counts its exports (builtinValue of a subclass's instance answers too)."] [33 1 "// Count is the exports held (a view not released, or not yet found dead)."] [36 1 "// Refuse is the exporter's check before it changes its buffer's size: nil while nothing holds an export (after the"] [37 1 "// collector found the views dropped unreleased dead), else BufferError msg (arraymodule.c's \"cannot resize an array"] [38 1 "// that is exporting buffers\", bytearray's \"Existing exports of data: object cannot be re-sized\")."] [49 1 "// Acquire and Release are a native's own export over a call (PyObject_GetBuffer ... PyBuffer_Release), for an"] [50 1 "// exporter whose buffer must not move while the call holds it."] [65 1 "// exportsOf is o's count, nil when o (or the built-in value of a subclass's instance) counts none."] [76 1 "// managedBuffer is _PyManagedBufferObject: one export of an exporter, shared by the views made from the first."] [78 23 "// the exporter's count (nil: the exporter counts none)"] [79 23 "// the views registered and not released (mbuf->exports)"] [80 2 "// a class's __buffer__ (PEP 688): the exporter whose __release_buffer__ gets the view __buffer__ returned"] [85 1 "// newManagedBuffer is the export memoryview(o) takes: o's count raised when it counts."] [89 3 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: no view is ever found dead, so none counts (pyi's behaviour before 249)"] [96 1 "// register makes v a view of mb (mbuf_add_view): it holds the export until released or dead."] [107 1 "// drop is mbuf_release: the export given back once the last view went."] [121 1 "// memoryviewFinalize is memory_dealloc's release of a view never released: its export given back."] [133 1 "// exportsVerify is the collection at a refused resize: Go's collection and the finalizers' drain (finRound) while it"] [134 1 "// gives exports back, within the collections' budget; whether e still exports (false also past the budget, or while"] [135 1 "// finalizers are draining: the resize then allowed). A count found held is confirmed until it moves."] [162 1 "// exportsRound is finRound's collection with a shorter wait: Go's collection, then a wait until a dead object is"] [163 1 "// queued or Go's finalizers have been still for 3 ms (polled every 100 us), then the drain. A view dropped unreleased"] [164 1 "// is queued as soon as Go's finalizer goroutine runs, so the common case (a temporary view) costs the collection"] [165 1 "// alone; a view still held costs the 3 ms once (BufferExports.confirmed)."] [189 2 "// exportsSpent is the time the refused resizes' collections took: held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time and"] [190 2 "// 200 ms, the moment at del's rule (finSpent, queue 222) with a budget of its own"] [192 2 "// PYI_EXPORTS_DEBUG=1: each verification's rounds on stderr"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[67 32] [70 46] [128 23] [145 16] [145 38] [170 28] [170 57] [178 28]]} (go/file "buffer_export.go" :imports [


